FFI-01 - unknown ABI

WHAT   An `extern` declaration names the calling convention
       it uses, in a string: `extern "C" fn ...`.
WHY    The convention decides how arguments are passed, who
       cleans the stack, and where the return value lands.
       Only the C ABI is implemented, so any other name is a
       promise the compiler cannot keep.
BAD    extern "Win64" fn abs(x: i32) -> i32;
GOOD   extern "C" fn abs(x: i32) -> i32;
NOTE   The ABI string is mandatory: `extern fn ...` without
       one is a syntax error (SYN-05), never a default.
